{{- /* internal/render/templates/toolbar.gohtml — the filter toolbar
(§5.3, §5.4): expand-all/collapse-all, priority/category/lens filter
chips, the visible-versus-total count, the "filter active" banner, and
the one-action reset. Hidden by default (report.css's ".toolbar {
display: none }", bead .5's own rule); shown only once report.js's
first statement adds the "js" class to <html> — it has nothing to
enhance without the script that drives it (§5.2), which is why this is
the one piece of markup allowed to disappear rather than degrade in
place.

This define emits only the toolbar's fixed chrome: the action buttons,
the count and banner elements, and one empty, labelled container per
facet. It does NOT enumerate priority/category/lens values itself —
"one chip per value actually present among this report's own findings"
(§5.3) is a runtime fact about which data-priority-css / data-category-css
/ data-lens values this page's own <details class="finding"> elements
carry, not something this Go template can determine without a helper
function bead .6 is not permitted to add (constructor injection lives in
non-template Go files this bead does not own). report.js populates
these three containers itself, at runtime, by scanning the DOM the
server already rendered — still zero interpolated data reaching the
static script (§5.1): every chip's value comes from a data-* attribute
already constrained to an enum member or an integer, read back out of
the DOM after html/template's own escaping already ran, never out of a
template action in this file or that one.

The inline <style> block below is this bead's own presentation for
elements only this file introduces (the buttons, chip row, count and
banner) — it is not report.css, so bead .5's ownership of that file is
untouched, and it reuses report.css's existing custom properties
(--panel-bg, --panel-border, --text, --text-muted, --link, --chip-bg)
rather than inventing a parallel palette. §9 (no network, no external
assets) is why this stays inline rather than a linked stylesheet, same
as every other style block on the page.

Dot is the root htmlView (report.gohtml calls {{template "toolbar" .}}),
but nothing below reads any of its fields — the facet containers are
populated by report.js, not by this template — so no caller-authored
byte flows through this file either. */ -}}
{{define "toolbar"}}
<div class="toolbar" id="toolbar" aria-label="Filter and view controls">
<style>
.toolbar-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; margin: 0.4rem 0; }
.toolbar button { font: inherit; cursor: pointer; border: 1px solid var(--panel-border); background: var(--panel-bg); color: var(--text); border-radius: 0.3rem; padding: 0.25rem 0.7rem; }
.toolbar button:hover { border-color: var(--link); }
.toolbar-count { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
.toolbar-banner { background: var(--chip-bg); border: 1px solid var(--panel-border); color: var(--text); border-radius: 0.4rem; padding: 0.4rem 0.7rem; margin: 0.4rem 0; font-weight: 600; }
.toolbar-facet { align-items: flex-start; }
.toolbar-facet-label { color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.8rem; min-width: 4.5rem; padding-top: 0.25rem; }
.toolbar-chip-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.35rem; }
.chip[aria-pressed="true"] { outline: 2px solid var(--link); outline-offset: 1px; }
</style>
<div class="toolbar-row toolbar-actions">
<button type="button" id="expandAllBtn">Expand all</button>
<button type="button" id="collapseAllBtn">Collapse all</button>
<button type="button" id="resetFiltersBtn">Reset filters</button>
<span id="filterCount" class="toolbar-count" aria-live="polite"></span>
</div>
<p id="filterBanner" class="toolbar-banner" hidden aria-live="polite"></p>
<div class="toolbar-row toolbar-facet">
<span class="toolbar-facet-label">Priority</span>
<div id="facetPriority" class="toolbar-chip-row" role="group" aria-label="Filter by priority"></div>
</div>
<div class="toolbar-row toolbar-facet">
<span class="toolbar-facet-label">Category</span>
<div id="facetCategory" class="toolbar-chip-row" role="group" aria-label="Filter by category"></div>
</div>
<div class="toolbar-row toolbar-facet">
<span class="toolbar-facet-label">Lens</span>
<div id="facetLens" class="toolbar-chip-row" role="group" aria-label="Filter by lens"></div>
</div>
</div>
{{end}}
